{
  "name": "Burn captions into a video with CaptionPipe",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-00",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -912,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 592,
        "height": 960,
        "content": "## Burn captions into a video with CaptionPipe\n\nDrop in a video URL or a binary file and get back the same video with the captions burned in, plus SRT, VTT, ASS and word timings. One HTTP node starts the job, a bounded poll loop waits for it, and a single error branch catches both API refusals and failed jobs.\n\nNo FFmpeg node, no self-hosted render, no monthly plan. [CaptionPipe](https://captionpipe.com) is hosted and prepaid: $10 buys 250 minutes, they never expire, and a failed job is not charged. New accounts get 5 free minutes.\n\n### Which path do I want?\n\nLeave `sendTheFile` **off** when the video is reachable on the public internet. That is one call, and CaptionPipe fetches it. Turn it **on** when the URL is one your n8n can reach but CaptionPipe cannot, an internal host for example: n8n fetches it and uploads the bytes itself.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The **Settings** node holds `videoUrl`, the `preset` look, the `sendTheFile` switch and the `maxPolls` budget.\n2. **Sending a file?** reads that switch and picks one of the two paths.\n3. The poll loop re-checks the job every 5 seconds, up to `maxPolls` times, then gives up rather than spinning forever.\n4. Success returns five links plus the seconds charged. Every refusal and every failed job lands in the one error branch.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Create an API key in the [CaptionPipe dashboard](https://app.captionpipe.com/connect). A new account includes 5 free minutes.\n- [ ] Add a **Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`.\n- [ ] Select it on the four HTTP Request nodes that call the API.\n- [ ] Put a video link in **Settings > videoUrl** and run it.\n\nFull docs: [captionpipe.com/docs](https://captionpipe.com/docs?client=n8n)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-02",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Send the bytes yourself\n\n**Use this when only your n8n can reach the URL**, an internal host for example. Claim a slot, fetch the video, PUT the raw bytes, start the job. Swap **Get the bytes** for a Drive or S3 node to send a real file."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-03",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 652,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Or just send the URL\n\n**Use this when the video is public.** One call, [CaptionPipe](https://captionpipe.com) fetches it itself, and n8n never moves the bytes. Fewer steps, so prefer it when you can."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-04",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1552,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Wait for the job\n\nBoth paths meet here. **Accepted?** separates a refusal from a live job. The loop waits 5 seconds and re-checks, up to `maxPolls` times, then stops."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-05",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2720,
        224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 492,
        "height": 580,
        "content": "## What comes back\n\nFive links on success: MP4, SRT, VTT, ASS and word timings, plus the seconds charged. Or a clean give-up if the poll budget ran out first."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-06",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2720,
        864
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## One error branch\n\nRefusals and failed jobs both arrive here, sorted into out of minutes, worth retrying, and nothing to retry. A failed job is never charged."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-07",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -288,
        752
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 568,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "## The webhook is open as shipped\n\nAnyone who has this URL can spend your caption minutes. Add authentication to the webhook node, or keep the URL private, before you activate the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-08",
      "name": "Sticky Note8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -288,
        960
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 660,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## Driving it from the webhook\n\nActivate the workflow, then POST to its production URL. Only `videoUrl` is required.\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://YOUR-N8N-HOST/webhook/5f2a1c84-3b7e-4d19-9a60-8c4e1f2b7d33 \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\n    \"videoUrl\": \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\",\n    \"preset\": \"highlight\",\n    \"sendTheFile\": false,\n    \"maxPolls\": 60\n  }'\n```\n\nThe webhook responds with the last node, so the request stays open until the job finishes and returns the five links."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
